.TH MAILWOMAN 1 "" "mailwoman 9.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mailwoman \- calibrated, retrieval\-augmented postal\-address parser and geocoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailwoman
[command] [options]
.br
.B mw
[command] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parse postal addresses into labeled components, geocode them against local sealed
data artifacts, and manage the reference databases those lookups read. The
.B mw
binary is an alias for
.BR mailwoman .
Every command answers
.B \-\-help
with more detail than this page; the sections below cover the commands an installer
runs directly. Maintainer surfaces (corpus, eval, gazetteer, release) are documented
in the repository.
.SH COMMANDS
.nf
Usage: mw <command> [options]

Commands:
  autocomplete      Complete a place\-name prefix from the FST gazetteer.
  clients
  corpus
  coverage
  data
  dev
  doctor            Check runtime, model, and optional data readiness.
  eval
  filer
  gazetteer
  geocode           Turn an address into a coordinate.
  gnaf
  license           Mint, issue and verify commercial license keys.
  openapi           Emit the native API OpenAPI document.
  parse
  placer
  poi
  registry
  release
  reverse           Resolve a coordinate to its administrative hierarchy.
  serve
  situs
  skill
  tiger
  tiles
  wof

Options:
  \-h, \-\-help        Show help.
  \-v, \-\-version     Show version.
.fi
.SH PARSE
.nf
Usage: mw parse <address...> [options]

Label the parts of an address — house number, street, locality, postcode — without looking anything
up: the output is your input, segmented and tagged. `mailwoman geocode` runs this same parse, then
resolves those parts against the gazetteer to produce a coordinate.

Arguments:
  address                   Formatted postal address

Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-debug                                     Enable verbose output (default: false)
  \-\-input\-mode <string>                       Input register
  \-\-locale <string>                           BCP\-47 locale (default: en\-US)
  \-\-default\-country <string>                  Resolver country scope
  \-\-country\-scope <string>                    Locale country\-scoping policy (default: auto)
  \-\-[no\-]admin\-coherence                      Joint admin consistency (default: true)
  \-\-[no\-]postcode\-country\-coherence           Postcode country consistency (default: true)
  \-\-postcode\-shape\-coherence                  Postcode shape consistency (default: false)
  \-\-postcode\-containment\-coherence            Postcode containment reranking (default: false)
  \-\-neural                                    Use neural\-only path (default: false)
  \-\-[no\-]poi                                  Enable POI query detection (default: true)
  \-\-download\-weights                          Download missing weights (default: false)
  \-\-degraded                                  Run structural stages only (default: false)
  \-\-format <string>                           Output projection (default: json)
  \-\-model <string>                            Explicit model path
  \-\-tokenizer <string>                        Explicit tokenizer path
  \-\-policy <string>                           Repeatable component policy override
  \-\-resolve                                   Resolve parsed nodes against WOF (default: false)
  \-\-resolve\-db <string>                       WOF SQLite distribution
  \-\-[no\-]street\-evidence\-rerank               Rerank street from atlas evidence (default: true)
  \-\-candidates <number>                       Alternative resolutions per node
  \-\-benchmark <number>                        Benchmark iteration count
.fi
.SH GEOCODE
.nf
Usage: mw geocode [address...] [options]

Turn an address into a coordinate: parse it, then resolve the parts against the gazetteer and the
rooftop/interpolation databases.

Arguments:
  address                   A formatted postal address to geocode. Omit when using \-\-stdin.

Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-locale <locale>                           Locale tag matching a weights package, such as en\-US
                                              or fr\-FR. (default: en\-US)
  \-\-bias <points>                             Soft proximity\-bias points: lat,lon[:weight];lat,lon.
  \-\-default\-country <country>                 ISO\-3166 resolver country scope; pass none to disable
                                              it.
  \-\-country\-scope <string>                    Apply the locale\-inferred resolver scope
                                              automatically, always, or never. (default: auto)
  \-\-resolve\-db <path>                         WOF admin SQLite distribution.
  \-\-candidate\-db <path>                       Demo\-parity byte\-range candidate database.
  \-\-data\-root <path>                          Root containing the address\-point, interpolation, WOF,
                                              POI, and other data databases.
  \-\-address\-points\-db <path>                  Explicit address\-point SQLite database, bypassing
                                              region selection.
  \-\-interpolation\-db <path>                   Explicit interpolation SQLite database, bypassing
                                              region selection.
  \-\-interp\-calibration <multiplier>           Force one interpolation uncertainty calibration
                                              multiplier.
  \-\-locale\-country\-prior                      Use a withheld locale country as a soft resolver
                                              ranking prior. (default: false)
  \-\-[no\-]gazetteer\-prior                      Feed the gazetteer FST prior to the parse;
                                              \-\-no\-gazetteer\-prior disables it. (default: true)
  \-\-[no\-]place\-country                        Use the coarse\-placer country prior;
                                              \-\-no\-place\-country disables it. (default: true)
  \-\-[no\-]postcode\-country\-coherence           Allow coherent postcode/locality evidence to override
                                              a wrong country scope. (default: true)
  \-\-[no\-]fork\-entity                          Probe POI data for exact entities when a fork parse
                                              does not resolve. (default: true)
  \-\-postcode\-shape\-coherence                  Opt into postcode shape exclusion/demotion. (default:
                                              false)
  \-\-postcode\-containment\-coherence            Opt into postcode\-centroid locality reranking.
                                              (default: false)
  \-\-[no\-]admin\-containment\-rerank             Region\-qualifier containment reranking of locality
                                              candidates; \-\-no\-admin\-containment\-rerank disables it.
                                              (default: true)
  \-\-capital\-tier                              Bounded national\-capital promotion on bare city names
                                              (default on); \-\-no\-capital\-tier disables it.
  \-\-variant\-alias\-exemption                   Own\-name variant aliases keep their holder's rank in
                                              cross\-country contests (default on);
                                              \-\-no\-variant\-alias\-exemption disables it.
  \-\-place\-country\-threshold <probability>     Coarse\-placer abstention threshold. (default: 0.9)
  \-\-format <string>                           Output format. (default: json)
  \-\-json                                      Shorthand for \-\-format json. (default: false)
  \-\-text                                      Shorthand for \-\-format text. (default: false)
  \-\-jsonld                                    Shorthand for \-\-format jsonld. (default: false)
  \-\-debug                                     Open the interactive parse/resolution/map view.
                                              (default: false)
  \-\-debug\-size <COLSxROWS>                    Frame size for non\-TTY debug rendering. (default:
                                              120x36)
  \-\-stdin                                     Read one address per line and emit one JSON object per
                                              line using one warm session. (default: false)
  \-\-timing                                    Write startup, initialization, and per\-address phase
                                              timings to stderr. (default: false)
  \-\-tiles <path>                              PMTiles archive for the debug map pane.
.fi
.SH AUTOCOMPLETE
.nf
Usage: mw autocomplete [prefix...] [options]

Return ranked place\-name completions for a prefix from the FST gazetteer.

Arguments:
  prefix                    Prefix string to complete.

Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-limit <number>                            Maximum number of completions. (default: 10)
  \-\-fst <path>                                FST binary; defaults from $MAILWOMAN_FST_BIN.
  \-\-json                                      Emit { engine, entries } as JSON instead of formatted
                                              text. (default: false)
.fi
.SH DOCTOR
.nf
Usage: mw doctor [options]

Check whether this machine can run mailwoman, and what each gap costs you. Runtime first (node,
ONNX), then the model weights, then the optional data layers geocoding needs — a missing layer is
reported, never fatal, and every failing line carries the one command that closes it. Then the
license posture: the branch of mailwoman's license that applies to this installation, and the
obligations each attached layer's recorded license carries (attribution, share\-alike, source offer).


Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-json                                      Emit the report as JSON instead of a checklist: {
                                              checks: [{ id, label, status, detail, consequence?,
                                              fix?, core }], exitCode } — a superset of { id,
                                              status, detail, fix? } (label + core + consequence aid
                                              machine consumers). With \-\-verbose, an `environment`
                                              array of { key, value, source } is added. (default:
                                              false)
  \-\-verbose                                   Also print every path and environment variable the
                                              checks resolved (data root, candidate.db, WOF
                                              databases, weights) so a surprising verdict can be
                                              traced to the setting that caused it. No \-v short
                                              form: the root program owns \-v for \-\-version.
                                              (default: false)
.fi
.SH DATA
.nf
Usage: mw data [options]

Fetch the reference databases geocoding needs — far too large to ship inside the npm package. `data
\-\-list` shows what exists, `data pull <bundle>` downloads one, `data status` reports what is already
on disk, and `mailwoman doctor` names the one you are missing.


Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-list                                      List every downloadable bundle (default: false)
.fi
.SH SERVE
.nf
Usage: mw serve [options]

Run the Mailwoman HTTP server


Options:
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show command help.
  \-\-port <number>                             Port to listen on (default: 3000)
  \-\-host <string>                             Network interface to bind (default: 0.0.0.0)
  \-\-cpus <number>                             Worker processes. Default: every available core
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAILWOMAN_DATA_ROOT
Root directory for the reference data artifacts (candidate gazetteer, POI layer,
street extracts). Defaults to a platform data directory; `mailwoman doctor \-\-verbose`
prints every resolved path.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://mailwoman.ai
.br
Issues: https://github.com/sister-software/mailwoman
